%description:
nodebHeight was a parameter of the channel model: one base station height for every link of a
carrier, whatever the positions of the base stations were. The height of a link's base station
end is now its antenna's. An ini file that still sets the parameter would be ignored without a
message, and the simulation would silently run with other heights than it asks for. Setting it
is an error at initialization.

%#--------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
%inifile: omnetpp.ini
[General]
network = simu5g.test.moduletest.lib.NrSessionTestNetwork

**.nrChannelModel[*].nodebHeight = 10m

include ../../lib/defaults.ini

%#--------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
%exitcode: 1
%#--------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
%contains: stderr
The 'nodebHeight' parameter is no longer used: the heights of a link are those of its two antennas
%#--------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
